cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use any Trinity FPGA discoveries, please cite our defensive publication."
title: "Zero-DSP FPGA for Ternary Inference"
abstract: "This bundle presents Trinity's comprehensive FPGA research for ternary neural network inference, featuring zero-DSP ternary MAC units (pure LUT implementation), DSP48E1 ternary wrappers (70% resource reduction), CORDIC with continued fraction approximation (6-stage sacred trigonometry), streaming argmax (<100 LUT), ternary BRAM storage (2-bit packing), power-of-2 embedding lookup, phi-weighted ternary scheduler, ESP32 Wi-Fi JTAG cross-platform programming, UART echo verification with LED feedback, OpenXC7 Docker synthesis pipeline, GF16 15-bit multiplier, and vector-matrix DSP acceleration for ternary matrix multiplication. All innovations published as defensive prior art with Zenodo DOIs."
